---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import ArticleFrame from '../components/ArticleFrame.astro';
const toc = [
  { id: 'acceptable-use', label: 'Acceptable use' },
  { id: 'files', label: 'Your files & outputs' },
  { id: 'availability', label: 'Availability' },
  { id: 'conversion', label: 'Conversion limitations' },
  { id: 'liability', label: 'Liability' },
  { id: 'changes', label: 'Changes' },
];
---
<SiteLayout title="Terms of Use | ConvertAnyFile" description="Terms for using ConvertAnyFile, including user responsibility, local image, archive and structured-data outputs, browser limitations, and service availability.">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="site-container hero-inner"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span>Terms</span></div><span class="eyebrow">Terms of use</span><h1>Simple terms for a simple converter.</h1><p>Use ConvertAnyFile for files you have the right to process, keep important originals, and verify converted outputs before relying on them.</p></div></section>
<ArticleFrame toc={toc}>
  <h2 id="acceptable-use">Acceptable use</h2><p>You may use ConvertAnyFile for lawful file conversion. You are responsible for ensuring that you have the rights and permissions needed to process the files you select and for complying with laws or contractual obligations that apply to your files.</p>
  <h2 id="files">Your files and outputs</h2><p>The current local converters do not intentionally take ownership of your source files or generated outputs. Conversion creates new output copies and can alter compression, metadata, color representation, animation, transparency, table structure, line endings, field representation, archive metadata, or other format-specific properties.</p><p>Review important outputs before using them in production, archival, publishing, data-import, backup, deployment, or other workflows where fidelity matters. Keep the original source when loss of metadata, transparency, animation, schema details, data types, archive permissions, ownership, links, extended attributes, or other format-specific features would be costly.</p>
  <h2 id="availability">Availability and supported formats</h2><p>The site may change supported formats, batch limits, runtime libraries, or browser requirements as the platform evolves. A file extension listed by the interface does not guarantee that every damaged, unusual, encrypted, or nonconforming variation can be processed successfully.</p><p>Browser-first conversion depends on the device, browser, available memory, and the category engine. Image support can depend on runtime codecs. Structured Data requires valid UTF-8 and follows documented conversion rules rather than custom schemas or ETL mappings. Archive support depends on container integrity, supported compression features, safe paths, browser expansion limits, and the metadata that can be represented in the target archive format.</p>
  <h2 id="conversion">No guarantee of perfect conversion</h2><p>File formats are complex. Some files may be damaged, use unusual codec variants or encodings, exceed browser memory, contain password protection, or include features that the target format cannot represent. A failed or imperfect conversion is possible.</p><p>Image format conversion is not restoration, upscaling, archival verification, or forensic recovery. Structured-data conversion is not schema validation, database migration, formula execution, type inference, or business-rule transformation. Archive conversion is not backup verification and does not promise preservation of symbolic links, hard links, ownership IDs, ACLs, extended attributes, sparse-file metadata, or vendor-specific metadata. A new extension does not guarantee that every property of the source is representable in the output.</p>
  <h2 id="liability">Liability</h2><p>Use the service at your own discretion and keep backups of important originals. ConvertAnyFile is not intended to replace professional archival, forensic, medical, legal, financial, engineering, regulated-data, or other high-stakes file-processing systems where independent validation is required.</p>
  <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2><p>These terms may be updated as the platform expands. Continued use after changes means you are using the service under the current published terms.</p>
</ArticleFrame>
</SiteLayout>
